  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8226974",
      "title": "Introducing useEffect's Cleanup Function",
      "sourceHash": "d1216cf30a3b1e0288492982196563486d72b0ea8b533c0d4d3b33dd36169306",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.3,
          "end": 1.35,
          "en": "Now, it's worth noting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.35,
          "end": 4.14,
          "en": "that this code here, of course, again in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.14,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "is a side effect because it's not directly related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 10.233,
          "en": "to outputting this JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.52,
          "end": 15.03,
          "en": "And useEffect can fix this timer problem I showed you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.03,
          "end": 17.91,
          "en": "in the previous lecture because with useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.91,
          "end": 20.1,
          "en": "we can actually stop this timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.1,
          "end": 22.62,
          "en": "when this component disappears.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.62,
          "end": 24.36,
          "en": "And I'll show you how.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.36,
          "end": 28.36,
          "en": "So, let's import useEffect from React here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.31,
          "end": 31.11,
          "en": "and let's then set the timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.11,
          "end": 35.91,
          "en": "with help of useEffect by providing this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.91,
          "end": 38.34,
          "en": "and our dependencies array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.34,
          "end": 40.65,
          "en": "And now we can move this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.65,
          "end": 42.183,
          "en": "into this effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.1,
          "end": 48.09,
          "en": "And now just to be clear, for setting this timer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.09,
          "end": 51.6,
          "en": "we would not need this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.6,
          "end": 55.59,
          "en": "because setting the timer wasn't the problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.59,
          "end": 58.71,
          "en": "Neither does this create an infinite loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.71,
          "end": 62.34,
          "en": "as we did it with the user location earlier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.34,
          "end": 65.04,
          "en": "nor do we have the problem we faced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 67.56,
          "en": "in the modal where we needed to work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 70.503,
          "en": "with some ref that wasn't connected yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.61,
          "end": 74.64,
          "en": "Instead here the problem is not setting the timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.64,
          "end": 77.58,
          "en": "but cleaning it up, getting rid of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.58,
          "end": 80.52,
          "en": "when this component function disappears.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.52,
          "end": 84.78,
          "en": "And that is also something useEffect can help you with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.78,
          "end": 88.26,
          "en": "because when using useEffect, you cannot just define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.26,
          "end": 92.97,
          "en": "this effect function, but also a cleanup function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.97,
          "end": 95.88,
          "en": "that should be executed right before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 97.863,
          "en": "this effect function runs again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.91,
          "end": 103.53,
          "en": "And you define such a cleanup function by returning it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.53,
          "end": 106.023,
          "en": "from inside the effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.92,
          "end": 111.03,
          "en": "So, this effect function can return another function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.03,
          "end": 114.78,
          "en": "which will then be executed by React right before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.78,
          "end": 117.96000000000001,
          "en": "this effect function runs again or,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.96000000000001,
          "end": 120.33,
          "en": "and that's the important part here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.33,
          "end": 123.45,
          "en": "right before this component dismounts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.45,
          "end": 126.063,
          "en": "So, before it's removed from the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.01,
          "end": 130.74,
          "en": "And therefore it's here in this cleanup function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.74,
          "end": 133.113,
          "en": "where we can now stop the timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.07,
          "end": 136.23,
          "en": "To do that, we can use the browser's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.23,
          "end": 139.89,
          "en": "built-in clear timeout function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.89,
          "end": 143.52,
          "en": "which now just needs a reference of the timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.52,
          "end": 145.02,
          "en": "that should be stopped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.02,
          "end": 149.73,
          "en": "And thankfully, such a reference is returned by set timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.73,
          "end": 152.76,
          "en": "So, we can simply store it in a constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.76,
          "end": 157.76,
          "en": "maybe named timer, and then pass timer to clear timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.67000000000002,
          "end": 162.6,
          "en": "And this will now stop this timer whenever this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.6,
          "end": 165.09,
          "en": "is removed from the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.09,
          "end": 167.37,
          "en": "Now, I also just again want to emphasize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.37,
          "end": 170.49,
          "en": "that this cleanup function would also run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.49,
          "end": 173.31,
          "en": "if that effect function would run again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.31,
          "end": 176.43,
          "en": "then the cleanup function runs right before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.43,
          "end": 178.17000000000002,
          "en": "the effect function runs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.17000000000002,
          "end": 180.54,
          "en": "But this is not something that can happen here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.54,
          "end": 183.24,
          "en": "because currently I have no dependencies here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 183.24,
          "end": 186.273,
          "en": "and therefore this effect function never runs again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.26,
          "end": 189.96,
          "en": "Now as you see, I'm actually getting a warning here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 189.96,
          "end": 193.53,
          "en": "So, I should add a dependency, to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.53,
          "end": 196.41,
          "en": "it's this unconfirmed prop which I'm using in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 196.41,
          "end": 199.07999999999998,
          "en": "that should be added as a dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 199.07999999999998,
          "end": 202.74,
          "en": "but I'm deliberately not doing that just yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.74,
          "end": 205.023,
          "en": "And I'll explain why in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.07,
          "end": 208.2,
          "en": "Instead, let's keep this code like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 211.2,
          "en": "and therefore the cleanup function will run only once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 213.42000000000002,
          "en": "when the component is removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.42000000000002,
          "end": 216.873,
          "en": "And let's save everything and reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.8,
          "end": 222.32999999999998,
          "en": "Now with that, if we wait for the sorted places to arrive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.32999999999998,
          "end": 224.67000000000002,
          "en": "I can add some places, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.67000000000002,
          "end": 228.15,
          "en": "And if I now open this and click no,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.15,
          "end": 233.15,
          "en": "you see the timer was set, but we don't have that problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.4,
          "end": 237.39,
          "en": "that we faced before that the place is magically removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.39,
          "end": 240.63,
          "en": "because the timer expires behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.63,
          "end": 243.15,
          "en": "This is not happening anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.15,
          "end": 246.9,
          "en": "because we're cleaning up that timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.9,
          "end": 251.16,
          "en": "We can console log cleaning up timer here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 251.16,
          "end": 254.313,
          "en": "just to see that in action, kind of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 255.27,
          "end": 258.81,
          "en": "If I reload and I click here and I click no,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.81,
          "end": 261.423,
          "en": "you see cleaning up timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.26,
          "end": 265.68,
          "en": "It's also worth noting that this cleanup function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 265.68,
          "end": 268.92,
          "en": "does not run right before the effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.92,
          "end": 271.5,
          "en": "is executed for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.5,
          "end": 275.1,
          "en": "It's only executed before subsequent executions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.1,
          "end": 276.51,
          "en": "of this effect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.51,
          "end": 279.39300000000003,
          "en": "and as mentioned, when this component is removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 280.47,
          "end": 283.62,
          "en": "And with that, we're now managing the timer as such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.62,
          "end": 287.373,
          "en": "that we don't cause any strange bugs in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}